$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=9={\\sigma }_{1},$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=4={\\sigma }_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the nonzero singular values of $A$ are ${\\sigma }_{1}=9$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186400772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400771 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e0b9d051-ab23-5d38-8461-85040e182756" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400772 #edb/ref 1080 "$9$ and $4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400772 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400772 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47ade149-2321-54bc-8689-575d0021aa81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400773 #edb/ref 1080 "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400773 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400773 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0322f6ef-5cd8-5b08-95d5-f8a6bea015f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400774 #edb/ref 1080 "$9{v}_{1}$ and $4{v}_{1}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56994b9b-ba0c-523d-9995-ad7e4cb025c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [